WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:18.783
hurried into the gym with her beach bucket.

2
00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:23.005
It was her first day back at camp after vacation.

3
00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:25.086
"Should we hide these?"

4
00:00:25.506 --> 00:00:26.307
she asked Mr.

5
00:00:26.347 --> 00:00:29.128
Dunn. "Before everyone else gets here?"

6
00:00:30.144 --> 00:00:32.066
He looked into the bucket of seashells.

7
00:00:32.086 --> 00:00:34.287
"Yep. Let's go!"

8
00:00:36.709 --> 00:00:37.430
Izzie and Mr.

9
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.011
Dunn went out to the playground.

10
00:00:39.971 --> 00:00:43.614
They hid Izzie's shells under the swings and behind the soccer goals.

11
00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:47.797
They hid more shells around the basketball nets and trees.

12
00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:51.260
They finished just as the other campers arrived.

13
00:00:53.141 --> 00:00:54.602
On the blacktop Mr.

14
00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:56.444
Dunn explained the day's activity.

15
00:00:57.612 --> 00:01:00.494
"Today you'll hunt for secret treasures.

16
00:01:01.655 --> 00:01:03.176
I can't tell you what they are."

17
00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.398
"Then how are we supposed to find them?"

18
00:01:06.718 --> 00:01:07.539
Bobby asked.

19
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.720
Mr. Dunn grinned.

20
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.902
"I'll give you a clue.

21
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:15.564
The treasures are from the sea.

22
00:01:16.685 --> 00:01:19.847
When you've found five items, bring them to the table."

23
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:22.209
"Yeah," Izzie added.

24
00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:25.011
"We're going to make something cool!"

25
00:01:25.031 --> 00:01:26.532
"Good luck!"

26
00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:30.869
Mr. Dunn waved the hunters off.

27
00:01:35.252 --> 00:01:38.193
clue wasn't very helpful," Jason complained.

28
00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:40.855
"Yes it was.

29
00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.657
I know what we're hunting for," Bobby bragged.

30
00:01:44.677 --> 00:01:46.918
"I figured it out!"

31
00:01:48.519 --> 00:01:51.841
Just then Nina shouted, "I found something!"

32
00:01:53.502 --> 00:01:56.063
The boys ran to Nina, who was by the swings.

33
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.772
"Watch where you step!"

34
00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.453
she squealed.

35
00:01:59.473 --> 00:02:01.594
"They're delicate!"

36
00:02:01.614 --> 00:02:03.356
"What are?"

37
00:02:03.776 --> 00:02:04.777
Jason asked.

38
00:02:05.857 --> 00:02:07.298
Nina opened up her hands.

39
00:02:07.318 --> 00:02:09.260
"The seashells."

40
00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:14.744
Once the campers knew what they were looking for, the seashells were easy to find.

41
00:02:16.365 --> 00:02:18.366
Soon they were all at the table.

42
00:02:18.386 --> 00:02:21.689
"We've got our seashells," Ethan said.

43
00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:23.010
"Now what?"

44
00:02:24.411 --> 00:02:25.471
"Well," Mr.

45
00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:29.879
Dunn said, "Izzie kindly collected these seashells from the beach for us.

46
00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.802
And her dad drilled tiny holes in each one.

47
00:02:37.185 --> 00:02:39.487
So I'll let her explain today's craft."

48
00:02:40.508 --> 00:02:42.009
Izzie beamed proudly.

49
00:02:42.029 --> 00:02:45.052
"We're making sea-breeze wind chimes."

50
00:02:46.573 --> 00:02:47.754
She held up a chime.

51
00:02:47.774 --> 00:02:50.657
"My family made this one last year.

52
00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.360
It has four shells and one piece of sea glass.

53
00:02:55.444 --> 00:02:57.105
And this is real driftwood."

54
00:02:57.125 --> 00:03:00.585
"What's driftwood?"

55
00:03:00.986 --> 00:03:01.686
asked Bobby.

56
00:03:01.706 --> 00:03:05.807
"Wood that's been floating in the sea for a while," said Ethan.

57
00:03:05.827 --> 00:03:10.188
"I brought you guys some driftwood too," Izzie added.

58
00:03:10.208 --> 00:03:12.889
"Thanks," Nina said.

59
00:03:12.909 --> 00:03:15.290
"How do we make the chimes?"

60
00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.090
"It's easy.

61
00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:21.251
You just have to tie everything to the wood," Izzie said.

62
00:03:21.271 --> 00:03:23.952
"First we have to make the hanger.

63
00:03:25.252 --> 00:03:28.293
Cut a piece of string about sixty centimeters long.

64
00:03:30.253 --> 00:03:33.194
Tie one end of the string around one end of your stick.

65
00:03:34.295 --> 00:03:38.216
Then tie the other end of the string to the other end of the stick.

66
00:03:39.356 --> 00:03:43.677
Now we're ready to attach the shells to the chime.

67
00:03:44.137 --> 00:03:50.939
Cut five pieces of string about thirty centimeters long each.

68
00:03:50.979 --> 00:03:54.500
Thread one string through the hole in one shell and knot it.

69
00:03:55.616 --> 00:03:58.757
Then tie the other end of the string to the driftwood.

70
00:03:59.638 --> 00:04:04.540
Keep doing this until all your shells are hanging down from the wood."

71
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.822
The campers laid out their shells, cut string, and got to work.

72
00:04:10.942 --> 00:04:13.103
"Make sure the knots are tight," Mr.

73
00:04:13.143 --> 00:04:13.784
Dunn said.

74
00:04:13.804 --> 00:04:18.085
"Hey, Izzie, thanks," Ethan said.

75
00:04:18.105 --> 00:04:21.407
"This reminds me of the beach in California."

76
00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:24.288
"You're welcome," Izzie said.

77
00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.084
She tied a small pink scallop shell to her wind chime and smiled.

78
00:04:30.085 --> 00:04:33.708
Today she shared a fun part of her beach vacation with her friends.

79
00:04:34.809 --> 00:04:37.312
And that felt as cool as a sea breeze!
